{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 Helvetica;}}\f0\fs24 {\b Topology}\par Visual Studio Code (CREATE) -> Google Docs (CREATE)\par \par {\b Request}\par One of the junior engineers on my team has put up a change that adds automatic retries to our refund service, and I need to review it before it goes anywhere near production. In Visual Studio Code I'll go through the changed files in the Source Control view and read the diff, then run the existing tests from the Testing panel. I'm worried a retry after a timeout could refund a customer twice, so I'll add one small test that shows it, run it and see it fail. Then in Google Docs I'll write my review feedback for the engineer: what they did well, what has to change before merge, and one thing to learn from it. Deliverables are the new failing test file and the review feedback as a PDF.\par \par {\b Task Description}\par 1. In Visual Studio Code, open the Source Control view and read the diff for each changed file: the config, the refund service and the tests.\par 2. In Visual Studio Code, run the existing tests from the Testing panel and show they all pass.\par 3. In Visual Studio Code, create a new test file with one test where the processor makes the refund but the response is lost, run it and show it fails because the customer is refunded twice.\par 4. In Google Docs, fill in the review template with the decision, what's good, the two must-fix items, a nice-to-have and a learning note for the engineer.\par 5. In Google Docs, download the review as a PDF.\par }